Runtime dependencies
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Entries are added as each package is actually referenced. Until Stream 0
creates the projects, this section lists what the plan commits to using, so
nothing is forgotten — but it is not yet a statement about shipped binaries.

  Avalonia .......................... MIT          (planned)
  Avalonia.Controls.DataGrid ........ MIT          (planned)
  CommunityToolkit.Mvvm ............. MIT          (planned)
  OpenCvSharp4 ...................... Apache-2.0   (planned)
  OpenCvSharp4.runtime.win .......... Apache-2.0   (planned)
  FlashCap .......................... Apache-2.0   (planned)
  .NET runtime ...................... MIT          (bundled by self-contained publish)

Note on the OpenCvSharp native runtimes: the NuGet packages declare
Apache-2.0, but the native binaries statically link or ship third-party
libraries including FFmpeg (LGPL-2.1+, or GPL-2+ when built with --enable-gpl).
Both upgrade cleanly into GPLv3, so this is compatible — but the specific
notices those libraries require have not been enumerated here. Chase this
before promoting a release widely.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Card data and images are retrieved from Scryfall (https://scryfall.com) under
its API terms. LoreFetch ships only DERIVED fingerprints and card names — no
Wizards of the Coast imagery is redistributed in this repository or in any
build artifact.

